AB  -  The purpose of the pilot PARTUM trial is to determine whether it is feasible to conduct a larger randomized controlled trial to determine whether low‐dose aspirin is efficacious and safe at preventing postpartum venous thromboembolism (VTE) in women at increased risk of VTE, compared to placebo. Given the large sample size needed to adequately power a large multicenter trial that assesses the efficacy of aspirin 81 mg versus placebo, the investigators first need to determine if it is possible to recruit enough women. If the pilot trial is successful and there are no major changes to the study design, then the secondary clinical outcomes collected in the pilot trial will be used in the analysis of the full multicenter trial.
