AB  -  There is a high risk of pulmonary embolism (PE) in patients with lung cancer, but no studies have identified which class of anticoagulants.It is best suited for patients with asymptomatic pulmonary embolism (UPE) lung cancer.The aim of this study was to investigate the efficacy and safety of sodium fondaparinux and warfarin for the prevention of UPE in patients with lung cancer.Patients with unexpected pulmonary embolism and lung cancer diagnosed by imaging between January 2016 and January 2019 were enrolled 80 patients who were randomly divided into group A and group B based on to the randomized control principle, with 40 patients in each group.Group A patients were given 3 4 mg of warfarin orally on the first 3 days (half dose was enough for the frail elderly and diabetic patients).The maintenance dose of 2.5 5 mg per day could be given after 3 days (the dose could be adjusted according to the clotting time to make the INR value reach 2 3).Patients in group B were treated with 7.5 mg sulfadoxine‐heparin subcutaneously once daily for 90 days.This was followed by a 1‐year follow‐up to investigate the treatment effect, hemodynamic parameters, recurrence of pulmonary embolism and adverse effects in both groups of patients etc.The results showed that the overall effectiveness rate of the two groups of patients treated with warfarin was 53.75% in group A, the overall effective rate of treatment with fondaparinux sodium was 83.75%, and the difference between the two groups was statistically significant (P< 0.05).Meanwhile, compared with the pre‐treatment period, the PaO2, PaCO2 and D‐dimer levels of the two groups were significantly improved after treatment.The difference was statistically significant (P< 0.05), while the comparison between the two groups was not significantly different (P> 0.05).In addition, the recurrence rate of pulmonary embolism in warfarin‐treated group A was 52.50% and the incidence of adverse events was 32.5%, while the recurrence rate of pulmonary embolism treated with fondaparinux sodium was 47.50% and the incidence of adverse events was 10%, there was a significant difference between the two groups (P< 0.05).In comparison with warfarin, sodium fondaparinux had better therapeutic efficacy in the treatment of accidental pulmonary embolism in patients with lung cancer and reduced patient's adverse reactions.It had a good clinical application.
