AB  -  INTERVENTION: Intervention1: Multicenter Randomized controlled trial: Consecutive adult patients with symptomatic DVT with or without associated Pulmonary embolism fulfilling inclusion criteria will be eligible to participate. All participants will receive anticoagulation as per standard of care for the initial 3 months. The type of anticoagulant will be at the discretion of the primary treating physician. At the end of three months, they will be randomized using computer generated sequence of random numbers to two arms â?? fixed duration and flexible duration arms. The randomization will be stratified based on study site and provoked/unprovoked VTE. The two arms will receive further anticoagulation as follows: The fixed duration arm will receive additional 3 months of anticoagulation (in case it is unprovoked DVT) or not receive any more anticoagulation (in case it was a provoked DVT). The flexible arm will be subjected to repeat ultrasound at 3, 9 and 15 months (if the DVT was unprovoked) or at 3 and 9 months (if the initial DVT was provoked). If at any of these time points the thrombosed vein is found recanalized, anticoagulation will be discontinued. If residual vein thrombosis is detected at any of these time points, anticoagulation will be extended till the next due date of scanning. In either case, maximum duration of anticoagulation will be 15 months in unprovoked and 9 months in provoked DVT. Follow up scans in those on flexible arm will be done using PoCUS by trained staff. At each follow up visit in these patients, a formal venous study will also be performed by a radiologist blinded to the PoCUS findings as well as the patient details. The sensitivity and specificity of PoCUS to detect residual venous thrombosis will be determined by comparison with the formal venous stud CONDITION: Health Condition 1: I829‐ Embolism and thrombosis of unspecified vein PRIMARY OUTCOME: 1.Recurrent VTE ; 2.Major bleedingTimepoint: 1.30 months from randomization. ; 2.30 months from randomization. SECONDARY OUTCOME: Sensitivity and specificity of PoCUS compared to formal venous scanning for detection of residual ; venous thrombosisTimepoint: 30 Months INCLUSION CRITERIA: Adults >18 years diagnosed with acute lower limb DVT with or without associated pulmonary embolism
